From 1c5c76ae7f371606d97ac7d5bd3027a9de9d4b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:41:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] core, web: the Controls page reads the hardware file
 through GET /api/config

Why: get_controls was a second door to the hardware file. It ran in a
second dispatcher before the command lock, parsed the file eight times
and wrote the error and warning counters from a read. Original Apertar
serves a read that must not wait for the lock as an HTTP GET route on
the web server's thread, and GET /api/config already returns this
file (buildHardwareConfigFileJson, App:5290-5321 and App:7168-7173
@upstream-1.6.0).

What: buildHardwareConfigFileJson is now an ApertarCoreApp member. It
keeps the upstream fields (ok, path, display_path, exists, size_bytes,
size_text, modified_text, text) and the port's revision and boot_copy,
and adds what get_controls sent: written_by, written_at, errors,
warnings, issues, replaced, model, peripherals, i2c_buses, apply,
dpi_lines, gpio_chips. It parses the file once. The model, peripherals
and issues are of the file Core runs; text stays the editor's text
(file, /boot copy or template). The systemctl probe stays in
controlsApplyJson. The get_controls block and its help entry are gone,
and the read no longer writes controlsErrors_/controlsWarnings_ (the
worker and the saves keep them). loadControls and controlsRecheckSoon
fetch /api/config with cache: "no-store"; loadControls still asks for
/api/config and list_actions together in one Promise.all.

Tested: check_core.sh both tests: PASS (warning counts unchanged).
--simulate with the controls fixture and with no hardware file:
/api/config carries every 1.6.0 field with the same type plus the
new members; Settings > Controls renders the same rows, the Hardware
card the same 7 peripherals as the build before this commit, no page
errors; Playwright: the first load sends GET /api/config and
list_actions side by side, a reload only GET /api/config. smoke_core.sh before/after: only get_controls (now Unknown
command), help (one name fewer) and the added /api/config members
differ. Needs the camera: open Settings > Controls while a take runs;
the page loads and curl -s localhost:8000/api/state shows
recording_dropped_frames 0.

